1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:07,475
A fresh captain trades, hires an escort, crosses a live ambush window with every unit of cargo intact, and sells at the destination.

2
00:00:07,475 --> 00:00:10,680
Every order shown here is a real NEAR testnet transaction.

3
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:15,218
For this recording, an automated wallet approves only the game contract methods.

4
00:00:15,218 --> 00:00:18,202
The full-access testnet credential never enters the page.

5
00:00:18,202 --> 00:00:21,710
This fresh captain then registers through the redesigned interface.

6
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:25,889
The captain spends 400 CRED on Blockspace and builds a defence-one sloop.

7
00:00:25,889 --> 00:00:29,980
The market quote and resulting inventory both come from the deployed contract.

8
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:33,697
A second fresh captain has built a galleon with exactly three defence.

9
00:00:33,697 --> 00:00:37,930
The convoy looks up that live offer and hires it through the interface before departure.

10
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:44,301
A scripted rival has exactly two idle defence, above the sloop alone but below the escorted convoy's total defence of four.

11
00:00:44,301 --> 00:00:50,860
Its committed and revealed ambush window is established first; then the captain loads every unit and departs inside that exact window.

12
00:00:51,210 --> 00:00:53,984
The contract resolves the voyage after the route distance.

13
00:00:53,984 --> 00:01:02,400
The proof compares the loaded ship cargo with the captain's credited inventory, alongside the exact rival power and window, rather than inferring protection from an event flag.

14
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:06,918
At Solana Reef, the captain sells every surviving unit through the live market.

15
00:01:06,918 --> 00:01:11,191
The final state confirms the Blockspace inventory was sold after arriving intact.

16
00:01:11,191 --> 00:01:15,570
The sale price is whatever the live market pays; this voyage is not a profit claim.

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:17,367
Now the captain turns raider.

18
00:01:17,367 --> 00:01:24,600
The idle sloop sets an ambush on the Bitcoin Isle to Solana Reef route with a window opening in 10 blocks, then springs it through the interface.

19
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:34,961
The capture record links every transaction and records the escort's defence, rival's complete fresh fleet, ambush bounds, exact departure block, and equal loaded and arrived cargo.

20
00:01:34,961 --> 00:01:38,020
This is live testnet evidence, not a simulated outcome.
